BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:LiveMusicAsheville.com
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260528T210000
DTSTAMP:20260528T001825
CREATED:20260520T100759Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260520T100759Z
UID:10063609-1779991200-1780002000@livemusicasheville.com
SUMMARY:Country Club Thursdays! | Prime Country
DESCRIPTION:Head to the showroom for live country and southern rock\, partnered up with $5 beer\, $10 old-Fashioned & espresso martini specials! No cover. \nDoors 5PM\nBands ⬇️ 6PM \n\nGet ready for a night of pure country power with Prime Country\, a band built to bring the hits to life. Led by a Nashville recording artist with the kind of voice that fills a room and hits you right in the chest\, they blend top-tier musicianship with a whole lot of heart.\nTwin guitars spark and weave through every song\, the bass and drums keep the groove locked tight\, and the crowd can’t help but move. From sing-along classics to new-school anthems\, Prime Country delivers the full country experience\, loud\, lively\, and all kinds of unforgettable.\n\n  \nFitz\, she’s the party. Wolfe\, he’s the epicure. 2 levels\, 3 vibes. 🎶 Live Music |🍸Sips & Noms 🥪 | 🕹️ Artcade | 🗝️Speakeasy | Private Events \nFitz and the Wolfe is a cocktail and music venue shaped by the spirit of improvisation\, storytelling\, and the kind of nights that feel too good to end. Here\, every night brings a new soundtrack. Jazz\, swing\, honky-tonk\, and sometimes things a little more esoteric—if it moves people\, we book it. The music fills the space like a second heartbeat\, sometimes rowdy\, sometimes intimate\, always memorable. It’s not background noise. It’s the reason you’re here. fitzandthewolfe.com
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/country-club-thursdays-prime-country/
LOCATION:Fitz and the Wolfe\, 1 Battery Park Ave\, Asheville\, NC\, 28801\, United States
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Screenshot-2026-04-25-092304-e1777123589663.png
GEO:35.5954515;-82.5548502
